      "bbox_source": "nearest preceding non-caption layout block fallback",
      "body_blocks": [
        {
          "page": 27,
          "label": "text",
          "content": "mosomes segregate, and so half the sperm from a male carry the X chromosome and half carry the Y chromosome. Although the Y chromosome carries very few genes other than those involved in the determination of sex and male fertility, the X chromosome carries as full a complement of genes as any other chromosome. Genes on the X chromosome are called X-linked genes, and the important consequence of X linkage is that a recessive allele on the X chromosome in a male is expressed phenotypically because the Y chromosome lacks any compensating allele. For X-linked genes with two alleles, therefore, there are three female genotypes (AA, Aa, and aa) but only two male genotypes (A and a).",
          "bbox": [
            99.0,
            190.0,
            784.0,
            430.0
          ],
          "block_id": 2,
          "block_order": 1
        },
        {
          "page": 27,
          "label": "text",
          "content": "The consequences of random mating with two X-linked alleles are shown in Figure 2.7, where the alleles are denoted  $ X^{A} $ and  $ X^{a} $. Note that in females, which have two X chromosomes, the genotype frequencies are as given by the Hardy-Weinberg principle in Equation 2.1; in males, which have only one X chromosome, the genotype frequencies are equal to the allele frequencies.",
          "bbox": [
            96.0,
            428.0,
            782.0,
            553.0
          ],
          "block_id": 3,
          "block_order": 2
        },
        {
          "page": 27,
          "label": "table",
          "content": "<table><tr><td rowspan=\"4\"></td><td colspan=\"3\">Male gametes</td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\">X-bearing</td><td>Y-bearing</td></tr><tr><td>Allele</td><td>X^{A}</td><td>X^{a}</td></tr><tr><td>Frequency</td><td>p</td><td>q</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Allele</td><td>Frequency</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>X^{A}X^{A}</td><td>X^{A}X^{a}</td><td>X^{A}Y</td></tr><tr><td>p^{2}</td><td>pq</td><td>p</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Female gametes</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>X^{a}X^{A}</td><td>X^{a}X^{a}</td><td>X^{a}Y</td></tr><tr><td>q</td><td>q^{2}</td><td>q</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"5\"></td><td colspan=\"3\">Summed frequencies in zygotes:</td></tr><tr><td>Females</td><td>Males</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>X^{A}X^{A}: p^{2}</td><td>X^{A}Y: p</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>X^{A}X^{a}: 2pq</td><td>X^{a}Y: q</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>X^{a}X^{a}: q^{2}</td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>",
